      "text": "On Thursday, May 22, the U.S. Coast Guard interdicted and detained four Mexican fishermen engaged in illegal fishing and seized around 200 pounds of fish in federal waters off southern Texas. The crew of Coast Guard Cutter Joseph Doyle detected and interdicted the fishermen. In coordination with the Joseph Doyle and Sector Corpus Christi Command watchstanders, a Station South Padre Island boat crew took the fishermen into custody and transferred them to U.S. Customs and Border Protection for processing.\n\nRead more: https://t.co/WjPgj7q8hF\n\n@USCGHeartland \n@DHSgov\n#uscg",
      "text_resolved": "On Thursday, May 22, the U.S. Coast Guard interdicted and detained four Mexican fishermen engaged in illegal fishing and seized around 200 pounds of fish in federal waters off southern Texas. The crew of Coast Guard Cutter Joseph Doyle detected and interdicted the fishermen. In coordination with the Joseph Doyle and Sector Corpus Christi Command watchstanders, a Station South Padre Island boat crew took the fishermen into custody and transferred them to U.S. Customs and Border Protection for processing.\n\nRead more: https://www.news.uscg.mil/Press-Releases/Article/4196727/coast-guard-detains-4-mexican-fishermen-seizes-200-pounds-of-illegally-caught-f/\n\n@USCGHeartland \n@DHSgov\n#uscg",
