      "reply_to_account": null,
      "reply_to_account_id": null,
      "quoted_tweet_id": null,
      "retweeted_tweet_id": null,
      "text": "Another significant win in our operations to disrupt criminal and terrorist organizations.\n\nOn May 22, 2025, the Coast Guard Investigative Service  – as part of the multi-agency Panama Express Strike Force – successfully extradited seven leaders of Transnational Criminal Organizations (TCOs) from Colombia. These individuals, which include suspects affiliated with Tren de Aragua and the Sinaloa Cartel, are accused of trafficking thousands of kilograms of narcotics through the U.S. southern border. These investigations were initiated and advanced by information obtained through criminal prosecutions resulting from Coast Guard maritime interdictions.\n\nEach interdiction plays a vital role. This operation underscores the ongoing commitment and effectiveness of the Coast Guard and its interagency partners in protecting the homeland and combating transnational threats. From maritime interdictions to investigations to extraditions, the Coast Guard is directly impacting the ability of cartels and TCOs to smuggle illicit drugs into our communities.  #BorderSecurity #HSI #DEA #FBI #USCG #Partnerships  #CGIS\n\n@DHSgov",
      "text_resolved": "Another significant win in our operations to disrupt criminal and terrorist organizations.\n\nOn May 22, 2025, the Coast Guard Investigative Service  – as part of the multi-agency Panama Express Strike Force – successfully extradited seven leaders of Transnational Criminal Organizations (TCOs) from Colombia. These individuals, which include suspects affiliated with Tren de Aragua and the Sinaloa Cartel, are accused of trafficking thousands of kilograms of narcotics through the U.S. southern border. These investigations were initiated and advanced by information obtained through criminal prosecutions resulting from Coast Guard maritime interdictions.\n\nEach interdiction plays a vital role. This operation underscores the ongoing commitment and effectiveness of the Coast Guard and its interagency partners in protecting the homeland and combating transnational threats. From maritime interdictions to investigations to extraditions, the Coast Guard is directly impacting the ability of cartels and TCOs to smuggle illicit drugs into our communities.  #BorderSecurity #HSI #DEA #FBI #USCG #Partnerships  #CGIS\n\n@DHSgov",
